WEBVTT

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:05.650
Riding a bike...

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:08.810
feels so good.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.900
Oh, I know.
I'll go polish Ponta-kun.

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:31.130
I look forward to having fun with you...

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:32.860
Ponta-kun!

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:06.810
Well,

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:11.060
Hunger knock yesterday,
aching muscles today. Sounds rough.

00:02:12.070 --> 00:02:12.940
Umm...

00:02:13.310 --> 00:02:15.690
Thank you for yesterday.

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:19.430
I'm Kurata Ami, a freshman.

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:22.070
And I'm Niigaki Aoi, also a freshman.

00:02:22.070 --> 00:02:24.950
That's right. We didn't ask your names.

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:27.950
I'm Saijo Hinako. You can call me Hinako.

00:02:27.950 --> 00:02:30.030
And she's Yayoi.

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:31.670
I'm Ichinose Yayoi.

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:34.860
We're both third years. Nice to meet you.

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:36.670
Nice to meet you too.

00:02:37.210 --> 00:02:39.840
Sorry we caused so much trouble yesterday.

00:02:38.110 --> 00:02:42.590
Hinako-san and Yayoi-san are the same age?

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:42.590
Oh, don't mind it. We didn't do much.

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:47.350
But it's such a coincidence that we go to the same college.

00:02:47.350 --> 00:02:49.260
Yeah, what a surprise.

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:52.590
Something you want to say?

00:02:52.590 --> 00:02:55.130
No, no! Not at all!

00:02:55.130 --> 00:02:57.550
By the way, you ride a road bike?

00:02:57.550 --> 00:03:00.530
You wouldn't expect to see
wheels like that on a crossbike.

00:03:00.530 --> 00:03:02.300
That's right.

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:04.970
Those were Mavic road wheels, right?

00:03:04.970 --> 00:03:09.280
Yes, but I'm thinking of getting deep rim wheels soon.

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:11.300
Oh yeah, that's what you'd want to try next

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:12.670
I know the feeling.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:16.370
Sorry.

00:03:16.370 --> 00:03:18.420
Yes, Saijo here.

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:23.090
Okay, then I'll head over now.

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:29.100
Sorry, I have to go to the bike shop.

00:03:29.740 --> 00:03:30.940
The bike shop?

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:33.580
The light you ordered came in?

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:34.580
Yeah.

00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:38.070
Um, would you mind if I tagged along?

00:03:41.470 --> 00:03:42.570
Of course not!

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:52.000
This is... the high-end shop we came to last time.

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:55.150
Don't tell me... you plan to shop here?!

00:03:55.670 --> 00:03:57.450
What's with her?

00:03:57.450 --> 00:04:00.840
She's traumatized by the prices here.

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:08.710
Come with me.

00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:14.730
Impossible... No way I can afford it.

00:04:15.690 --> 00:04:17.740
See? How about this one?

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:21.550
What? There are bikes in this price range?

00:04:21.550 --> 00:04:24.340
And then there are ones like that.

00:04:26.260 --> 00:04:27.450
500 thous-?!

00:04:28.570 --> 00:04:31.370
Why are the prices so different?!

00:04:31.950 --> 00:04:35.170
They perform differently,
and there are some other factors, so...

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:38.920
It's shocking at first, huh? I was the same.

00:04:43.310 --> 00:04:46.430
The accessories on the first floor are fun to look at as well.

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:51.790
You're right! There are so many cute ones.

00:04:53.080 --> 00:04:55.560
This helmet is especially cute!

00:04:56.260 --> 00:04:58.750
See anything you're interested in?

00:04:58.750 --> 00:04:59.820
Yes!

00:05:00.310 --> 00:05:02.970
Hinako-san, what kind of light did you buy?

00:05:06.220 --> 00:05:07.070
This one.

00:05:09.690 --> 00:05:11.200
It's quite big, isn't it?

00:05:15.260 --> 00:05:16.220
Ami!

00:05:16.220 --> 00:05:18.000
Why did you look straight into it?

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:19.590
Oh my...

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:23.250
Were you able to browse around?

00:05:23.250 --> 00:05:25.340
Yes, it was fun!

00:05:25.900 --> 00:05:30.690
I didn't know you needed such bright lights for cycling.

00:05:30.690 --> 00:05:33.310
It's safer to have something that bright.

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:36.390
There are times you have to
ride at night, like during a brevet.

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:38.770
Brevet?

00:05:41.090 --> 00:05:46.520
A brevet is a type of long-distance cycling
with a set distance and specified time limit.

00:05:46.520 --> 00:05:50.570
Cycling through beautiful scenery without worrying about who's first.

00:05:50.570 --> 00:05:53.790
It's really fun.

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:56.530
And the mountain roads at night...

00:05:56.530 --> 00:06:01.540
are breathtaking when the sky is filled with stars.

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:07.440
And they're held in regions throughout Japan,

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:10.800
so you get to try all kinds of delicious food.

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:18.060
Not only that...

00:06:18.060 --> 00:06:22.730
There's a brevet known as a flèche for teams of up to five riders.

00:06:22.730 --> 00:06:24.360
As a team?

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:28.160
Flèche challenges only specify
the location of the finish,

00:06:28.160 --> 00:06:33.460
so you're free to set your own route, including
the starting point, and work your way to the goal.

00:06:33.460 --> 00:06:37.790
It's a wonderful form of cycling where you can
share moving experiences with your teammates.

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:40.470
We can all ride together?

00:06:40.470 --> 00:06:43.500
Yeah, and we can ride our very own course.

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:46.760
That's incredible...
That sounds like so much fun!

00:06:47.140 --> 00:06:50.910
I really want to participate in a flèche with everyone here!

00:06:50.910 --> 00:06:53.110
Aoi-chan, we should try it!

00:06:53.110 --> 00:06:55.100
W-Wait, Ami.

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:57.900
Do you really think it's okay to treat this so lightly?

00:06:57.900 --> 00:07:00.020
Sure!

00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:02.110
It's called "fresh",

00:07:02.110 --> 00:07:05.310
so it has to be a brevet for "fresh" beginners, right?

00:07:05.310 --> 00:07:08.940
Flèche means "arrow" in French.

00:07:10.540 --> 00:07:12.030
Oh... I misunderstood...

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:14.270
You didn't know, it's understandable

00:07:15.290 --> 00:07:20.920
Um, then, how far do you ride in a flèche, specifically?

00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:24.920
It's a brevet that lasts 24 hours and spans 360 kilos.

00:07:26.110 --> 00:07:26.670
What?

00:07:30.590 --> 00:07:35.680
O-Oh... I see...
I must have misheard you. Silly me.

00:07:36.170 --> 00:07:39.180
I'm sorry, but can you explain it to me once more?

00:07:39.450 --> 00:07:42.930
It's a brevet that lasts 24 hours and spans 360 kilos.

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:51.930
Th-That's impossible!

00:07:54.950 --> 00:07:58.990
Well, there's more to cycling than brevets and flèches.

00:07:58.990 --> 00:08:02.310
Oh yeah, are you free this weekend?

00:08:02.310 --> 00:08:03.460
Um, yes...

00:08:04.020 --> 00:08:08.550
We were talking about cycling around Miura this weekend.

00:08:08.550 --> 00:08:11.050
The coastline makes for such pretty scenery.

00:08:11.050 --> 00:08:13.130
If you're interested, would you like to join us?

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:17.890
Cycling along the coastline?

00:08:27.490 --> 00:08:30.740
I didn't know you could take your bike on a train.

00:08:30.740 --> 00:08:34.470
We call carrying bicycles onto trains like this "Rinkou".

00:08:34.470 --> 00:08:37.620
This allows you to cycle much further out.

00:08:37.620 --> 00:08:42.600
Yeah! I was wondering how we'd get to the meeting point.

00:08:42.600 --> 00:08:44.620
This is convenient and fun!

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:47.160
As long as we avoid peak hours,

00:08:47.160 --> 00:08:51.590
and are careful not to get in the way of the other passengers.

00:08:51.590 --> 00:08:53.260
Yeah, you're right.

00:08:53.760 --> 00:08:58.200
But we can take it to the touring location,
and we don't have to worry about the return home.

00:08:58.200 --> 00:08:59.260
I see!

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:01.420
Especially your folding bike, Ami.

00:09:01.420 --> 00:09:05.230
It's nice and easy to carry,
so you don't have anything to worry about.

00:09:05.630 --> 00:09:09.710
I'm so happy I can travel with Ponta-kun.

00:09:09.710 --> 00:09:14.880
This sense of ease is really great!
I think I feel my world broadening!

00:09:18.810 --> 00:09:20.370
We're here!

00:09:20.750 --> 00:09:23.620
Ami, you'll be in the way there.

00:09:26.480 --> 00:09:28.380
How about here?

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:29.380
Yeah.

00:09:29.380 --> 00:09:31.660
Well then, let's put them together.

00:09:31.660 --> 00:09:32.510
Okay!

00:09:38.730 --> 00:09:42.740
Your bike looks hard to assemble.

00:09:42.740 --> 00:09:46.010
Well, it's not that hard once you get used to it.

00:09:46.010 --> 00:09:49.100
I don't think I could ever manage that.

00:09:56.000 --> 00:09:57.610
I just had to have this one.

00:09:58.030 --> 00:10:00.870
With this, I'm a fellow cyclist!

00:10:02.090 --> 00:10:03.930
Even I'm a cyclist!

00:10:03.930 --> 00:10:05.740
It looks quite good on you.

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:10.960
But I'm not used to it yet,
so I feel a bit embarrassed.

00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:15.410
But if you plan on continuing, a helmet's a must-have.

00:10:15.410 --> 00:10:16.720
Yes!

00:10:21.870 --> 00:10:25.120
Hinako-san and Yayoi-san are late, aren't they?

00:10:25.120 --> 00:10:28.430
A few trains have already arrived.

00:10:29.730 --> 00:10:33.230
Sorry, we're late!

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:35.170
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:10:36.200 --> 00:10:37.610
You didn't come by train...?

00:10:38.040 --> 00:10:40.790
No, we rode straight here on our bikes.

00:10:40.790 --> 00:10:43.840
Do you live around here?

00:10:43.840 --> 00:10:46.400
Not at all. We live in Zama.

00:10:46.400 --> 00:10:49.960
So it's about 55 kilos away.

00:10:51.520 --> 00:10:53.180
Even though we're about to go cycling?

00:10:53.180 --> 00:10:54.630
This is nothing.

00:10:55.280 --> 00:10:56.880
They're too amazing.

00:10:56.880 --> 00:11:00.380
Hinako-san, what's our route for today?

00:11:00.760 --> 00:11:04.490
We'll just leisurely ride along the coastline.

00:11:04.490 --> 00:11:08.450
The sea breeze and the open scenery are so refreshing.

00:11:08.450 --> 00:11:11.900
Well, the rest should be a surprise for when we're riding.

00:11:11.900 --> 00:11:13.760
I can't wait!

00:11:13.760 --> 00:11:14.670
Yeah.

00:11:14.670 --> 00:11:17.920
Remember, always keep safety in mind.

00:11:17.920 --> 00:11:21.470
Stay on the left side of the road and never ride parallel.

00:11:21.470 --> 00:11:25.350
If you get tired, you can always stop and rest.

00:11:25.350 --> 00:11:26.660
Okay!

00:11:26.660 --> 00:11:27.910
All right!

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:30.410
I'll do my best!

00:11:43.310 --> 00:11:46.580
Huh? I smell the sea...

00:11:49.530 --> 00:11:51.420
It's the sea!

00:12:02.410 --> 00:12:03.820
Wow!

00:12:04.350 --> 00:12:07.330
The coastline goes on forever.

00:12:07.960 --> 00:12:10.330
It's easy to ride...

00:12:10.330 --> 00:12:13.220
and the sea breeze feels so good!

00:12:13.220 --> 00:12:15.210
This is the best!

00:12:17.710 --> 00:12:20.460
It felt so good just a little while ago...

00:12:20.960 --> 00:12:23.640
What is this hill?!

00:12:23.640 --> 00:12:26.470
Come on, we'll be over it in no time.

00:12:26.470 --> 00:12:28.970
Really?

00:12:28.970 --> 00:12:34.120
Really! Just don't push yourself.
Follow us at your own pace.

00:12:34.120 --> 00:12:35.400
Okay.

00:12:35.980 --> 00:12:40.070
They're so fast! This is what they call "leisurely"?

00:12:40.410 --> 00:12:44.050
But I can't be a burden on them today.

00:12:44.050 --> 00:12:45.320
I have to keep up!

00:12:47.830 --> 00:12:49.590
I'm dying...

00:12:49.590 --> 00:12:53.210
Oh no, I can't see them anymore!

00:12:53.870 --> 00:12:57.080
What'll I do...?

00:12:59.920 --> 00:13:00.960
Ami?

00:13:02.700 --> 00:13:04.720
What's wrong, Ami?!

00:13:07.870 --> 00:13:10.340
They left us behind.

00:13:10.340 --> 00:13:15.180
Don't worry. It's hard to match
someone else's pace on hills,

00:13:15.180 --> 00:13:17.150
so you don't have to force yourself.

00:13:17.840 --> 00:13:18.980
But...

00:13:18.980 --> 00:13:22.820
Hinako-san said to go at your own pace, right?

00:13:23.700 --> 00:13:24.820
Yeah...

00:13:24.820 --> 00:13:28.860
They're probably waiting for us at the top.

00:13:28.860 --> 00:13:30.080
Really?

00:13:30.430 --> 00:13:35.670
Overworking yourself and not being able to finish
would be even more troublesome.

00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:43.400
Then... how do I go up this hill?

00:13:44.510 --> 00:13:48.860
You just need to focus on climbing this hill
as comfortably as you can, Ami.

00:13:49.700 --> 00:13:51.190
I see...

00:13:51.190 --> 00:13:54.020
I'll try it. Please teach me, Aoi-chan.

00:13:54.800 --> 00:13:58.600
First, when going uphill, use your lowest gear.

00:14:00.110 --> 00:14:03.400
Stand on your bike and look straight ahead.

00:14:05.050 --> 00:14:08.110
It's okay to go slowly, but keep a steady pace.

00:14:08.640 --> 00:14:11.200
Okay, I think I can do this.

00:14:11.840 --> 00:14:12.990
But...

00:14:12.990 --> 00:14:14.670
I'm so slow!

00:14:16.250 --> 00:14:20.450
But it's much easier than earlier.

00:14:20.450 --> 00:14:23.210
It's slow, but I'm moving steadily!

00:14:24.540 --> 00:14:29.070
But... how long is this hill going to continue?!

00:14:34.040 --> 00:14:34.680
Oh...

00:14:35.560 --> 00:14:36.810
Here they come.

00:14:37.170 --> 00:14:38.170
Hey!

00:14:38.940 --> 00:14:41.800
Almost there! Keep going!

00:14:42.400 --> 00:14:44.320
Hang in there!

00:14:50.140 --> 00:14:51.720
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:14:51.720 --> 00:14:53.450
Good work.

00:14:53.450 --> 00:14:54.910
You made it!

00:14:55.770 --> 00:14:57.620
That was so cruel, Hinako-san!

00:14:57.620 --> 00:15:00.680
What part of that was "over in no time"?!

00:15:00.680 --> 00:15:01.680
You lied!

00:15:01.680 --> 00:15:05.750
Calm down. This is nothing compared to a mountain pass.

00:15:05.750 --> 00:15:08.090
That's not a fair comparison.

00:15:08.620 --> 00:15:12.970
But you managed to climb it.
You worked really hard.

00:15:13.660 --> 00:15:15.070
See, look.

00:15:17.470 --> 00:15:21.200
You made it all the way here with your own strength.

00:15:32.650 --> 00:15:34.870
Gives you a sense of accomplishment, huh?

00:15:35.540 --> 00:15:36.830
Yes!

00:15:36.830 --> 00:15:42.270
Good. I hate to spoil the moment,
but we don't have much time. Let's go.

00:15:43.100 --> 00:15:47.710
Um, I just finished this climb and I'm tired and... hey!

00:15:54.390 --> 00:15:57.970
I can't go any further...

00:16:01.500 --> 00:16:03.960
What is that? Is she motioning to me?

00:16:07.580 --> 00:16:09.440
I thought I was going to die!

00:16:09.440 --> 00:16:11.400
You sure lay it on thick.

00:16:11.400 --> 00:16:13.950
It's been downhill for a while.
You're okay, aren't you?

00:16:14.460 --> 00:16:17.700
No one warned me about that hill in the first place...

00:16:18.240 --> 00:16:21.210
And I was tired, but you didn't give me a chance to rest...

00:16:22.860 --> 00:16:27.730
Come on, we made it to our stop, so isn't it fine?

00:16:27.730 --> 00:16:29.980
What? Our stop?

00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:36.640
Let's eat then.

00:16:36.640 --> 00:16:37.640
I'm digging in!

00:16:43.050 --> 00:16:44.390
What is this? What is this?!

00:16:45.110 --> 00:16:47.400
The fish is really delicious!

00:16:53.990 --> 00:16:56.160
This is heaven!

00:16:56.560 --> 00:16:59.590
Ami-chan, you have such a happy expression!

00:16:59.590 --> 00:17:02.120
Wow, look at the line.

00:17:02.670 --> 00:17:05.010
If it's this delicious, I can see why though.

00:17:05.010 --> 00:17:08.130
Yeah, this place is packed during lunch.

00:17:08.500 --> 00:17:10.820
Aren't you glad we rushed to get here?

00:17:10.820 --> 00:17:12.340
Mmhmm...

00:17:14.920 --> 00:17:16.590
Thank you for the food!

00:17:17.080 --> 00:17:19.690
It was delicious!

00:17:20.850 --> 00:17:25.270
But I ate so much.
I might have put on some weight.

00:17:26.480 --> 00:17:28.430
Don't worry.

00:17:28.430 --> 00:17:33.780
You're burning calories with cycling.
Eating this much is nothing.

00:17:33.780 --> 00:17:36.440
Really? Thank goodness.

00:17:36.440 --> 00:17:41.760
But if you keep eating at this pace
without cycling, you'll have a big problem.

00:17:46.820 --> 00:17:50.090
Thank you for inviting us today.

00:17:50.090 --> 00:17:54.280
I wasn't expecting such a wonderful treat at the end.

00:17:54.280 --> 00:17:57.930
What're you saying?
The main event starts now.

00:17:57.930 --> 00:17:59.430
Huh?!

00:17:59.430 --> 00:18:03.260
We're not done riding? No way...

00:18:04.060 --> 00:18:06.850
It's really not that far from here.

00:18:06.850 --> 00:18:09.520
You rested up and your recovered your stamina, right?

00:18:09.520 --> 00:18:13.240
Well... yeah... but...

00:18:13.730 --> 00:18:17.600
Then let's stay focused and enjoy the ride until the very end.

00:18:18.220 --> 00:18:19.100
Okay.

00:18:19.900 --> 00:18:21.210
What's the matter, Ami?

00:18:22.830 --> 00:18:24.080
Oh, nothing.

00:18:39.630 --> 00:18:42.890
Ami, does your butt hurt?

00:18:44.440 --> 00:18:48.650
N-Not... really...

00:18:48.650 --> 00:18:50.480
That's not convincing...

00:18:51.390 --> 00:18:56.360
Hinako-san, Yayoi-san...
Can we stop?

00:18:56.720 --> 00:18:59.470
Ami's butt can't take anymore.

00:19:05.760 --> 00:19:08.160
You need to speak up if it hurts.

00:19:08.160 --> 00:19:09.920
But...

00:19:09.920 --> 00:19:13.060
Being embarrassed and saying nothing only makes it worse.

00:19:14.350 --> 00:19:18.670
This happens to every beginner.
Don't worry about it.

00:19:19.080 --> 00:19:21.570
Oh, really?

00:19:21.570 --> 00:19:24.030
Everyone goes through it.

00:19:24.530 --> 00:19:27.470
Ami, put this over your saddle.

00:19:27.910 --> 00:19:30.980
It's cushioned and should help.

00:19:34.480 --> 00:19:36.150
How is it?

00:19:36.150 --> 00:19:38.740
Much better, I think...

00:19:38.740 --> 00:19:41.340
It's just a bit more.

00:19:41.340 --> 00:19:42.720
Hang in there.

00:19:43.230 --> 00:19:44.740
Okay.

00:19:54.750 --> 00:19:57.560
It's better, but...

00:19:57.560 --> 00:20:00.240
It's still sore!

00:20:07.040 --> 00:20:11.440
Okay, when you go uphill...

00:20:11.440 --> 00:20:16.060
Drop it to the lowest gear and stand on your seat...

00:20:16.060 --> 00:20:18.320
and look straight ahead.

00:20:18.320 --> 00:20:21.550
It's okay to go slow, just keep a steady pace.

00:20:28.440 --> 00:20:29.950
Just a bit more.

00:20:29.950 --> 00:20:31.840
Almost there!

00:20:36.350 --> 00:20:38.880
Ami, this is the main event!

00:20:49.230 --> 00:20:50.640
Wow!

00:20:51.220 --> 00:20:53.470
You did it!

00:20:53.470 --> 00:20:54.770
Yup!

00:21:03.900 --> 00:21:05.970
I made it!

00:21:05.970 --> 00:21:07.280
Our destination!

00:21:07.280 --> 00:21:09.100
We made it!

00:21:09.100 --> 00:21:10.910
Nice work out there.

00:21:11.950 --> 00:21:13.910
That felt great.

00:21:14.620 --> 00:21:17.360
Mt. Fuji was amazing!

00:21:17.360 --> 00:21:18.530
Right?

00:21:18.530 --> 00:21:21.560
How's your butt?

00:21:21.560 --> 00:21:24.350
Oh, I forgot all about it.

00:21:25.800 --> 00:21:27.060
I see.

00:21:27.060 --> 00:21:32.560
Cycling through beautiful scenery makes you forget the bad things.

00:21:33.900 --> 00:21:36.060
That might be true.

00:21:36.060 --> 00:21:41.170
I feel like I rode an unbelievably long distance.

00:21:41.170 --> 00:21:43.530
I think we really did.

00:21:44.520 --> 00:21:46.450
I wonder how far we traveled?

00:21:47.080 --> 00:21:51.450
Today's total distance is about 55 kilometers.

00:21:53.200 --> 00:21:55.340
55 kilos?!

00:21:56.210 --> 00:21:59.170
I rode that far?!

00:21:59.170 --> 00:22:01.210
Surprising you can actually ride so far, right?

00:22:01.590 --> 00:22:03.200
You broke your record, huh?

00:22:07.110 --> 00:22:08.870
This is incredible...

00:22:08.870 --> 00:22:11.850
Even I can do it if I try.

00:22:11.850 --> 00:22:16.730
At this rate, you'll be able to go even further.

00:22:18.480 --> 00:22:19.840
Yes!

00:22:22.590 --> 00:22:24.730
Okay then, let's head back.

00:22:24.730 --> 00:22:29.110
Huh? Are you two going to cycle back?

00:22:29.110 --> 00:22:32.490
This is nothing on a road bike.

00:22:32.490 --> 00:22:35.750
You two are too amazing.

00:22:36.250 --> 00:22:37.710
We'll see you again.

00:22:37.710 --> 00:22:39.660
Be careful on your way home.

00:22:41.480 --> 00:22:44.880
Now then, let's pack up our bikes
and go home on the train.

00:22:45.260 --> 00:22:46.220
Yeah!

00:22:54.590 --> 00:22:55.840
Good morning!

00:22:56.740 --> 00:22:58.770
Oh, good morning!

00:22:58.770 --> 00:23:00.810
Oh, you're by yourself?

00:23:03.000 --> 00:23:06.320
Ami is bedridden with full-body muscle aches.

00:23:06.320 --> 00:23:07.340
Again?

00:23:07.340 --> 00:23:08.650
Oh my.

00:23:08.650 --> 00:23:14.990
I need to do something to prevent muscle pain
and protect my butt next time.

00:23:30.780 --> 00:23:34.220
I actually rode 55 kilometers... I'm so impressed!

00:23:34.220 --> 00:23:36.640
I really can do it if I try!

00:23:36.640 --> 00:23:39.930
Some day, I want to go on a
long-distance ride with everyone!

00:23:40.410 --> 00:23:44.320
Next time on Long Riders: "A New World."
